print("Assignment")

print("1. Explain the difference between git add and git commit in your own words. Why are both steps necessary?")
print("Answer: Git add tells the repository will be included in the next version. Git commit is a checkpoint to track down what changed in the next following versions. They are necessary because git add lets you select what goes with a commit while git commit records an update processed by the user.")

print("2. A classmate says: If I delete a committed file from Github, my local copy will also be deleted. Is this correct? What command would update the local copy?")
print("Answer: No, it will not be deleted immediately. A git pull will be used first to update the local for the modification to apply.")